adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts` the only auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET)
  return 403;
```

If `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset (i.e., `undefined`) and the request omits the header (so the indexed header value is also `undefined`), the condition is `false` and the request is accepted. That makes the route effectively unauthenticated in the “missing secret” misconfiguration case, and the handler can then create/update credentials for any existing `userId` (it only checks that the user/app exist). The additional notes about array-valued headers / casing are also grounded in how `req.headers[...]` can be `string | string[] | undefined` and is compared directly, but the main bypass when the secret is undefined is a concrete, verifiable issue in the diff.
